From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uku Kert Paidra <ukukert@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:24:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] elan: Wait for sensor to leave pre-scan after stopping capture

After a short swipe the driver reports a retry and sends stop_cmd
(0x00 0x0b), which has no response, and reports finger-off at once.
That re-enters calibration, which sends get_image_cmd about 1 ms later,
before the sensor has left its wait-for-finger state. On the 0x0c11
that image read hangs for ELAN_CMD_TIMEOUT and the enrollment fails
with a timeout.

Add a 10 ms settle state after stop_cmd, before stop_capture_complete()
reports finger-off.

[Apex: backport of draft MR !647, commit 7500a883c072, unchanged except
for context. Applies to v1.94.100 with or without the Apex patches 0001,
0002 and 0101. Apex carries it but does not enable it. Enable it only
when a debug log shows that the capture after a retry fails or times
out in calibration right after STOP_CAPTURE.]

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libfprint/libfprint/-/merge_requests/647
Refs: libfprint#817 #796 #601 #836 #348
---
 libfprint/drivers/elan.c |    7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
index 03576d568acb..8e5889ff0a5f 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
@@ -474,6 +474,7 @@ elan_run_cmd (FpiSsm                *ssm,
 
 enum stop_capture_states {
   STOP_CAPTURE,
+  STOP_CAPTURE_SETTLE,
   STOP_CAPTURE_NUM_STATES,
 };
 
@@ -488,6 +489,12 @@ stop_capture_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
       elan_run_cmd (ssm, dev, &stop_cmd,
                     ELAN_CMD_TIMEOUT);
       break;
+
+    case STOP_CAPTURE_SETTLE:
+      /* stop_cmd has no response, but the sensor needs time to leave
+       * pre-scan before another calibration can request an image. */
+      fpi_ssm_next_state_delayed (ssm, 10);
+      break;
     }
 }
 
